_vrf_PLAT971_shelx
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  2.05A   From I7              5.14 eA-3  
RESPONSE: The residual electron density existing near the Pb-I framework
is due to the fact that this structure is "collapsed", representing an
average structure where the F5PEA and PEA atoms are not separated in
space. As the F5PEA and PEA cations are different, it will lead to
slightly different Pb-I coordinates, hence resulting in the observered 
residual electron density. In an idealized structure, the Pb-I framework
will be slightly different when F5PEA is located near it versus when
PEA is.
;
_vrf_PLAT973_shelx
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Positive Resid. Density on       Pb1       2.57 eA-3  
RESPONSE: The residual electron density existing near the Pb-I framework
is due to the fact that this structure is "collapsed", representing an
average structure where the F5PEA and PEA atoms are not separated in
space. As the F5PEA and PEA cations are different, it will lead to
slightly different Pb-I coordinates, hence resulting in the observered 
residual electron density. In an idealized structure, the Pb-I framework
will be slightly different when F5PEA is located near it versus when
PEA is.
;
_vrf_PLAT201_shelx
;
PROBLEM: Isotropic non-H Atoms in Main Residue(s) .......          5 Report
RESPONSE: The signifigant amount of disorder within the cationic inter-
layer gallery arising from the two cations residing upon one another in
a 1:1 ratio prevents these atoms from being refined anisotropically. 
When done so, the ADPs increased drastically to unrealistic amounts.
Therefore, the non-PbI framework were refined isotropically.
;
_vrf_PLAT414_shelx
;
PROBLEM: Short Intra D-H..H-X       H01B     ..H2E              1.88 Ang.  
RESPONSE: As this is an average structure, the neighboring cations will
appear to be closer than they are; in the idealized (non-average)
structure, only specific cations can exist within a given cation
inter-layer gallery, which alleviates these short contacts.
;
